1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,688
We now have a connected path from text to a short persistent plan, from that plan to continuous Jewels, and from Jewels to video.

2
00:00:07,688 --> 00:00:12,276
We also know that persistent trajectories can preserve recognizable subjects.

3
00:00:12,276 --> 00:00:14,005
The missing piece is breadth.

4
00:00:14,005 --> 00:00:19,130
Today's subject and setting instructions still point back to specific training fields.

5
00:00:19,130 --> 00:00:26,400
A real model needs reusable ideas such as dog, walking, beach, and camera pan that can combine beyond their source videos.

6
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:32,814
Today, an instruction such as subject seven ultimately means material taken from one fitted training field.

7
00:00:32,814 --> 00:00:37,513
Adding thousands of source numbers would only build a larger filing cabinet of examples.

8
00:00:37,513 --> 00:00:42,853
Instead, we must discover patterns repeated across many videos and give those patterns shared names.

9
00:00:42,853 --> 00:00:47,980
A walking-dog instruction should be learned from many dogs and many walks, not tied to one clip.

10
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:54,408
Fit Jewel fields for at least one hundred videos covering ten to twenty prompts with useful combinations.

11
00:00:54,408 --> 00:00:59,100
Then learn sixty-four to two hundred fifty-six recurring subject and setting patterns.

12
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:05,101
Each pattern should own a connected path through time while reusing the existing shape and color vocabularies.

13
00:01:05,101 --> 00:01:09,138
Finally, reject any generated result that copies too much from one source.

14
00:01:09,138 --> 00:01:12,520
Passing this test would show genuine reusable building blocks.

15
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:17,428
A future language model should not recite every Jewel one at a time.

16
00:01:17,428 --> 00:01:26,771
It should speak a hierarchy, like a film crew's plan: scene and camera first, then persistent objects, then their paths, then local appearance details.

17
00:01:26,771 --> 00:01:32,092
Smaller specialist modules can expand that plan into exact Jewel positions and shapes.

18
00:01:32,092 --> 00:01:40,260
This lets the language model spend its capacity on meaning and long-range consistency rather than repetitive rendering instructions.

19
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:44,268
Long video will be generated in neighboring time windows.

20
00:01:44,268 --> 00:01:50,710
The model must carry state from one window to the next: object identity, position, direction, speed, and style.

21
00:01:50,710 --> 00:01:55,701
Speed and direction are derivatives, meaning measurements of how position is changing.

22
00:01:55,701 --> 00:02:00,866
Predicting those changes worked better than predicting every next position independently.

23
00:02:00,866 --> 00:02:06,960
It is the difference between continuing a thrown ball's flight and guessing a fresh location every frame.

24
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:15,499
Training and evaluation should split whole combinations, such as an object doing an action, instead of randomly splitting similar videos.

25
00:02:15,499 --> 00:02:19,276
Correct text must beat swapped-object and swapped-action controls.

26
00:02:19,276 --> 00:02:23,796
One prompt should produce several recognizable but genuinely different samples.

27
00:02:23,796 --> 00:02:29,805
A second time window must continue from the model's own carried state, without peeking at a target video.

28
00:02:29,805 --> 00:02:32,780
These checks separate composition from memorization.

29
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:37,649
More compute matters only when paired with the right data and structure.

30
00:02:37,649 --> 00:02:42,050
More varied videos reveal which objects, actions, cameras, and paths repeat.

31
00:02:42,050 --> 00:02:47,667
More training can turn those repetitions into shared concepts and learn how prompts combine them.

32
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:50,447
More rendering compute can improve local detail.

33
00:02:50,447 --> 00:02:54,095
The pitch is not that size will magically repair random splats.

34
00:02:54,095 --> 00:03:01,160
It is that the full route now works at toy scale, and the next uncertainty can be attacked directly with data and compute.
